course: dictionary
lesson: 15103
title: Runic: old letters and magic
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A rune is an old letter. The Vikings and Anglo-Saxons used runes to write before they used the Latin alphabet, the letters we use today. «The stone has a runic inscription carved along its edge.» Runic means written in runes, so this stone has old letters carved on it.
explain: Some words have a second meaning. In stories, «The wizard's runic marks began to glow blue.» Here runic means mysterious or magical, like old runes. Ask yourself: are the letters being read, or does the word sound magical? The clues in the sentence will tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Always check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The runic stone showed the name of a Viking chief.» Does "written in runes" fit? Yes, it does. Does "mysterious and magical" fit? Not really, so this sentence uses the first meaning.
fact: Runes are an old set of letters used by Germanic peoples, such as the Vikings and Anglo-Saxons.
fact: «Runic» means written in runes, or mysterious and magical, as in old stories.
fact: A «runic alphabet» is the set of runes, the old letters themselves.
fact: A «runic inscription» is writing carved on something, such as a stone.
fact: Runes were used before the Latin alphabet, which is the alphabet we use today.
exercise: «The museum has a runic stone from the Viking age.» What does runic mean here? | *Written in runes, an old set of letters | Made of gold and very shiny | Sung by children at school | Very new and painted bright blue
exercise: «The wizard waved his hand over the runic marks, and they began to glow.» What does runic suggest here? | Wet and muddy from the rain | Written in a school book | Very hungry after a long walk | *Mysterious or magical
exercise: Which phrase means the set of old letters called runes? | runic inscription | runic wizard | runic weather | *runic alphabet
test: Which peoples used runes, according to the facts? | Children in London today | *Vikings and Anglo-Saxons | Ancient Egyptians | Romans only
test: «The runic marks on the door made the children shiver.» What does runic mean here? | Painted bright red | Very old and broken | *Mysterious and magical | Written in runes, like a letter
exam: Clara says a runic stone is just an ordinary rock. Why is she wrong? | Because stones are never carved | Because runes are a kind of food | *Because a runic stone has old letters, called runes, carved on it | Because Clara has never seen a stone
